ESP32 Smart Room Monitoring & Control Dashboard

Aim

To develop a smart room monitoring and control system using ESP32 and DHT11 sensor with a web-based dashboard.

Components Required

- ESP32 Development Board
- DHT11 Temperature and Humidity Sensor
- Relay Modules
- LEDs / Lights
- Fan
- Jumper Wires
- USB Cable

Connections

Component| ESP32 Pin
DHT11 DATA| GPIO 4
Light 1 Relay| GPIO 16
Light 2 Relay| GPIO 17
Light 3 Relay| GPIO 18
Fan Relay| GPIO 19
DHT11 VCC| 3.3V
DHT11 GND| GND

Software Requirements

- Arduino IDE 2.3.11
- ESP32 Board Package
- DHT Sensor Library
- Adafruit Unified Sensor Library

Working

1. ESP32 creates its own Wi-Fi network named SmartRoom.
2. The DHT11 sensor measures room temperature and humidity.
3. ESP32 collects the sensor readings.
4. A web dashboard displays temperature and humidity values.
5. Users can control three lights and one fan using the dashboard.
6. Sensor readings are refreshed every 2 seconds.

Wi-Fi Details

- SSID: SmartRoom
- Password: 12345678
- IP Address: 192.168.4.1

Output

The dashboard displays:

- Light 1 ON/OFF control
- Light 2 ON/OFF control
- Light 3 ON/OFF control
- Fan 1 ON/OFF control
- Room Temperature
- Room Humidity

Applications

- Smart Homes
- Room Automation
- Smart Classrooms
- Remote Device Monitoring

Conclusion

The ESP32 Smart Room Monitoring and Control Dashboard provides a simple way to monitor room temperature and humidity and control electrical devices through a mobile phone or computer using Wi-Fi.
